<title>INDIA: India produces 4,290T copper cathodes in December.</title>
<headline>India produces 4,290T copper cathodes in December.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's state-run Hindustan Copper Ltd (HCL) produced 4,290 tonnes of copper cathodes in December 1996 compared to 4,190 tonnes in November, a governemnt statement said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>HCL also produced 5,051 tonnes of continous cast copper rods in December against 3,075 tonnes in November, the statement said.</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>	    Installed   December,1996    Cumulative output</p>
<p>	    capacity    -------------    -----------------</p>
<p>	    (annual)	 Actual	 Apr-Dec 96  Apr-Dec 95</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Copper</p>
<p> cathodes   47,500	 4,290	  26,757     28,642</p>
<p>Copper</p>
<p> rods	 60,000	 5,051	  31,131     24,010</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures are in tonnes and provisional.</p>
</text>
